{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1380818-is-using-no-realms-overpowered","id":1380818,"title":"Is Using No Realms Overpowered?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-12T18:48:33-07:00","id":1380818,"title":"Is Using No Realms Overpowered?","content":"I've always been a fan of Changeling's setting but the previous rules just never felt too appealing. It didn't help that I was often in mixed games so Changelings often felt a little underpowered when compared to other supernaturals. C20 though seems to have fixed a lot of those issues however. Before I started playing though I was wondering about making one, probably big, adjustment and doing away with Realms and making Arts more like Vampire Disciplines, assigning a relevant skill for the dice roll instead of adding dots for Realms. Am I overthinking how much Realms impact/limit powers and does doing away with them make Changelings too strong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T21:14:20-07:00","id":1380855,"title":"","content":"Realms are incredibly significant for Changeling cantrips, not only because they cover what they can readily do, but without them changelings have to bleed glamour for every dot beyond their own realms, which can really cause them to suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T21:28:22-07:00","id":1380858,"title":"","content":"Realms make arts much more versatile, having virtually every realm at maximum is really powerful. Imagine if other powers (Not talking about mage here) could be used with realms? Potence and celerity? Buff the entire coterie! Animalism 1? Instead of talking with animals why not use it to speak with objetcs, dead bodies, etc? Actually, primal 1 with the right realms already does that.<br /> <br /> Imagine using dominate to make a car door open, sovereign can do that. Imagine using methamorphosis to turn your enemy into a bat, well, methamorphosis (the art) can do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Arts are the most versatile powers of all splats with the exception of true mages. Exactly because of the realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T22:45:24-07:00","id":1380869,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Realms make cantrips ridiculously powerful. The only thing that tops them is Mage's Sphere-magick.<br /> <br /> Like, Sovereign is not only Dominate on steroids, but how you can apply it to targets other then another person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T07:47:53-07:00","id":1380942,"title":"","content":"What people have said, unless you are going to allow people to use Realms for free then, yeah Expect Changelings to own everything since that's &quot;I hit everyone in an appartment complex with Lightning&quot; level(or transform them into cows.. or..)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:45:15-07:00","id":1380976,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses. I think some experience playing will open this up for me. Even with a magic system Im used to Mage the Awakening and not Ascenscion so using two stats for powers is new. I\u2019m guessing doing away with the Realms is more like Dark Ages Fae which I see being talked about as overpowered all the time. Unleashing is also something I should utilize more too though I have all sorts of questions about scale when it comes to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T08:53:25-07:00","id":1381332,"title":"","content":"Unleashing was added in C20 (well, Dark Ages:Fae), and is wonkier in terms of both power scale and effects. I tried homebrewing something different accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],